							<td style="padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--fg-pencil); color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 600;">Number: 48–64pt Bold</td>
							<td style="padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--fg-pencil);">Center table stand / floral ring</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- SEO Article & Comprehensive Guide -->
		<article class="hand-card" style="padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); margin-bottom: 4rem;">
			
			<div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
				<span class="badge-postit">Reception Stationery & Seating Playbook</span>
				<h2 class="font-heading" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 42px); color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-top: 0.5rem; text-align: center;">
					The Complete Guide to Wedding Place Cards & Table Numbers
				</h2>
				<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 750px; margin: 0.5rem auto 0; text-align: center;">
					Place cards vs. escort cards, caterer meal indicator stamps, cardstock printing weights, and seating chart management.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQs -->
			<section>
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 2rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">
					Frequently Asked Questions
				</h3>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						How do I score and fold tent cards cleanly without creasing?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						To get a crisp, professional fold on heavy 100lb cardstock, use a ruler and a bone folder (or the back edge of a butter knife) to gently score the centerline before folding. This creates a sharp edge that stands upright without cracking the paper fibers.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
					<summary class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-blue);">
						Can I print table number centerpiece cards with this tool?
					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Yes! Change the format dropdown to <strong>"🔢 Table Centerpiece Cards (5x7)"</strong> and the tool automatically formats large, beautiful table centerpiece signs ready to insert into photo frames or floral stands.
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="faq-accordion" style="margin-bottom: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem; background: var(--bg-paper);">
